a Binary literal gives the bytes of the text of the string
a range up to an end plus one is the range that includes the end
a then value without else is nil where else nil is
a declaration without its empty value starts empty
a condition without its double negation holds where it did
a value without its cast to the type that it has is the value
a member alone or a record where its type is expected is the member or the construction
a field without its nil default takes nil where its argument is left out
a named argument written as the name alone is that argument
an emptiness test with is_empty holds where that of its length or of the empty text did
a membership test with in holds where contains does
an is test of a union holds where one of its members does
a value taken apart itself gives what the const that held it gave
an index without its bounds, or a range to an end plus one in a test, is the same
a declaration without the type that its value has holds the same value
a function without the types that it infers gives the same results
a Map or a Set with the type arguments of its declaration holds the same type
a construction of its one argument by its name constructs what its value alone does
the comparison that sorted takes by default sorts as none does
Set() of an array of an Iterable holds what Set() of the Iterable does
a Char added to a String appends what its to_string() does
a test that find finds none tells what any does
